    "result_text": "All 271 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created (or otherwise returned), the response now includes a `displayName` field formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema (which regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `displayName` getter/setter).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Mapped `displayName` via a MapStruct expression backed by a new `toDisplayName(Owner)` default method that returns `lastName + \", \" + firstName` (null-safe).\n\n3. **`src/test/java/.../OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 Extended `createOwnerSuccess` to assert `$.displayName` equals `\"Franklin, George\"`.\n\nThe controller's `addOwner` already maps the saved owner through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, so the computed display name flows into the create response automatically.",
